= Metadata — Technical =

== Metadata element sets ==
A metadata vocabulary defines properties such as:

<pre>
dc:title
dct:creator
dct:subject
dct:license
</pre>

Terms need identifiers, definitions and usage rules.

== Application profiles ==
An application profile can combine terms from multiple vocabularies and specify local constraints.

This separates:
* globally reusable vocabulary meaning;
* local requirements.

== Encoding ==
Metadata may be encoded in:
* RDF;
* XML;
* JSON;
* relational tables;
* embedded binary fields;
* specialized catalog formats.

Encoding does not determine semantics by itself.

== Controlled values ==
Metadata properties can use:
* free text;
* controlled vocabularies;
* authority files;
* URIs;
* datatypes.

Controlled values improve interoperability but can reduce expressive flexibility.

== Metadata crosswalks ==
A crosswalk maps terms between metadata schemas.

Mappings can be:
* exact;
* lossy;
* broader/narrower;
* conditional.

A one-to-one field mapping can hide different semantics.

== Provenance ==
Metadata transformations should themselves be recorded where important.

Otherwise, aggregation can lose:
* original source;
* timestamps;
* field meaning;
* confidence;
* transformations.

